/target

# The deep-review report this branch works through. Kept locally, not shipped.
perch-review.html

# What a Dogfood run writes: one dated report per run (ADR 0037). Never
# committed, because a report names the real Accounts it was run against —
# `tests/dogfood.rs` asserts this line is here rather than trusting it.
/dogfood-reports

# What `perch export` writes, and what `dogfood-setup` defaults to writing in
# the directory it was run from — which is this one. An Export holds a working
# Credential for every Account the machine has, so it is one `git add -A` away
# from a public history. `tests/dogfood.rs` asserts this line too.
*.age

# What renders the guide leaves behind: `mdbook serve docs` writes here, and
# `mdbook build docs --dest-dir _site/guide` is what the Pages workflow does.
/docs/book
/_site
